{"ld": 825, "paper": "SP345", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Prohibit Geoengineering, Including the Use of Cloud Seeding, Weather Modification, Excessive Radio Waves and Microwave Radiation", "sponsor_id": "s-black-russell", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-greenwood-randall"], "committee_code": "ENR", "committee_name": "Environment and Natural Resources", "summary": {"text": "This bill prohibits a person from engaging in any activity that constitutes or involves geoengineering. \"Geoengineering\" is defined in the bill as any intentional, large-scale intervention in Earth's natural systems and includes stratospheric aerosol injection; weather modification techniques; excessive electromagnetic, radio frequency or microwave radiation emissions; harmful nuclear, biological or chemical emissions; or other polluting atmospheric activity. The Department of Environmental Protection is charged with enforcing the prohibition, and a person that violates the prohibition commits a Class C crime and is subject to a fine of $500,000 for each day the violation continues and any other applicable penalties under the Maine Revised Statutes, Title 38 or other provision of law or rule.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0345&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "final_disposition": {"label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "date": "2025-05-14", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 825)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0345&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-66)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0345&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (S-66)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": null, "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?